    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Let G be a soluble group, and let A and B be periodic subgroups of G. Is\nit true that any subgroup of G contained in the set AB = {ab | a ∈ A, b ∈ B} is\nperiodic? This is known to be true if AB is a subgroup of G.      F. de Giovanni",
